    {
      "id": 5673567933527536,
      "plugin": "StochasticTelegraph",
      "model": "Fermata",
      "version": "2.0.30",
      "params": [],
      "rightModuleId": 5620206684685207,
      "data": {
        "text": "DOUBLE CROSS STEP\n=================\n\nTwo MINISTEPS run off triggers passing through MULT. Set their period lengths independently if you want. Step length is controlled by a CVMIX whose three attenuverters:\n\n1. Static voltage, unless you plug something in\n\n2. Feedback from this MINISTEP\n\n3. Cross-feedback from other MINISTEP\n\nAvailable at the end of the chain are:\n\n- Both MINISTEP outputs\n- Ring-mod product of the MINISTEP outputs\n- Gates from passing each of these through COMPARATORs\n\nadd feedback, add complexity\n \n",
        "width": 3,
        "screen_colors": 45848490672128,
        "font_choice": "fonts/RobotoMono-Bold.ttf",
        "visible_lines": 28,
        "title_text": "DOUBLE CROSS STEP"
      },
      "pos": [
        149,
        7
      ]
    },
